The class `DisposableAutoReleaseObserver` is a thin wrapper around a consumer with minimal logic (state check, try‑catch). Its performance is dominated by the user‑provided `Consumer` and the underlying RxJava infrastructure, not by any algorithmic work inside this class. Consequently, a dedicated JMH benchmark would not yield meaningful insights about this class itself, and creating a benchmark would add unnecessary maintenance overhead. Therefore, generating JMH benchmark code is not required.